WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.400
The first time

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.034
as President Joe

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.869
Biden gave the graduation speech

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.337
to the US Air Force Academy's

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.972
class of 2023

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.340
and just after all,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.475
the graduates had received

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.809
their diplomas.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.510
President Biden

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.212
appeared to trip and fall

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.647
as his heading back to his seat on stage.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.383
He appeared to land,

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.450
as you can see that video there

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.184
on his right hip.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.919
CNN's Priscilla Alvarez

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.422
joins me now live Priscilla.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.523
Following that fall

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.291
he seems to have gotten up,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.760
went back to his seat,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.194
seems to be doing okay.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.629
Do we know what happened? And we didn't.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.664
Do we know his date now? Right.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.533
I mean, he seemed to be in fine spirits

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.601
after returning to his seat.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.236
He was helped out by a group of men,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.771
including an Air Force official

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.739
and two Secret Service agents.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.874
But all of that after

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.043
what was a long five hour

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.678
ceremony where he had he had shaken hands

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.747
with the cadets

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.617
as they were graduating over 900 of them.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.451
So that came towards

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.819
the end of the ceremony.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.454
But really, the focus of the ceremony

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.356
and his commencement address

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.291
was focused on the world and the globe

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.659
and how it's changing.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.761
Abby, there are a lot of concerns

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.297
among voters, Democrats included,

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.133
about President Biden's age

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.269
and about his ability

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.371
to serve for six more years,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.205
five more years.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.974
And then there was an incident today.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.341
We shouldn't

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.242
make too big a deal out of it.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.611
We're told that he's not hurt

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.914
but it certainly doesn't help.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.182
He fell.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:22.782
He tripped

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.118
while walking during the Air Force

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.487
Academy commencement ceremony today.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.354
He tripped on something either

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.690
a sandbag or some sort of cable

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.192
or something.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.894
This this does come as he's facing

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.029
growing scrutiny

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:39.065
about his age and and wherewithal.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:40.500
Yeah.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.802
I mean, look, this is not good.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.571
It's not anything that the White House

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.606
or his campaign wants for two reasons.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:50.110
One, the optics of it are absolutely bad.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.012
But secondly, I mean, in general,

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.182
it is not good for

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.551
the president, especially one of

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.387
President Biden's age to take a fall.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.124
Falls are dangerous, actually,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.859
from a factual perspective.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:06.426
And so, look,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.460
this is not good news

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.027
for the White House.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:08.828
They don't want to be dealing

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:09.863
with this narrative.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.964
I've also been hearing

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.165
from a lot of Republicans

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.233
who are very eagerly,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.302
eagerly sending around old clips of,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.037
you know, articles

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.872
talking about when

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:22.775
Trump kind of tiptoed down a slope

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.411
and seemed to be worried

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.180
about falling in a situation

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.548
and how that was interpreted

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:29.516
by the media.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.717
I think the White House

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.518
is now going to be

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.152
dealing with something

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.153
they've been dealing with,

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:33.920
which is concerns

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.255
about the president's age,

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.257
but also Republicans in particular

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.758
trying to

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.126
make this a contrast

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.195
between Trump and Biden.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.297
And that's not the conversation

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.698
they want to have at all.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.500
So it hasn't happened.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.002
They'll have to deal with it.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.670
But but it's certainly not something

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.371
I think the White House

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.839
is particularly happy about, though.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.374
They couldn't do anything about it.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.011
It reminds me of a very different dynamic

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.978
when Bob Dole,

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.413
who was the presidential candidate

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.447
in for Republicans

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.616
in 1996, fell off a stage

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.150
and the media

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.552
made a big deal out of that obviously

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.253
very different age contrast

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.488
with incumbent President Bill Clinton.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.122
Thanks to all of you.

